From 32d6ab273e89923c6fea2fa8c415f8887b1da325 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Meadlock <jmeadlock@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:45:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dsv41): rotate decode queries on a rank dealt no index
 rows

Base: vLLM 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 plus the candidate-72
series (0001..0867).

Rationale:
1. The overlapped decode path (0767) defers q's RoPE and shared decode
   metadata to the aux stream and previously launched them inline inside
   select_rows' loop over this rank's index chunks, beside _index_chunk.
2. _decode_index_split deals a decode step's index rows across TP ranks
   (SPRows(rows, tp, rank): ceil(rows / tp) rows each, in rank order) once
   the step has 24 rows or more, or on an eager decode past 16,384 tokens.
3. When (tp - 1) * ceil(rows / tp) >= rows the last rank is dealt no rows
   (e.g. TP8 at 25..28, 33..35, 41, 42, and 49 rows; eager long-context TP3
   at 4 and TP4 at 5, 6, and 9 rows). _index_query returns empty queries for
   it, select() never enters the chunk loop, and the deferred _rope(q) never
   runs. On TP8 (where rank 7 owns 8 local heads), forward_mqa then attends
   with un-rotated queries on every layer with an indexer.
4. Extract _launch_pending_decode_aux() on DeepseekV4Attention and guard it
   with a single-shot issue_pending_aux() helper in forward_mqa that runs
   once per overlapped decode forward: beside the first _index_chunk on
   non-empty slices, right after select() before gather on empty rank-split
   slices (so RoPE overlaps with the all-gather), and before every
   wait_stream(pending_aux) join. This also prevents duplicate RoPE launches
   across multi-chunk scoring or _INDEX_SPLIT_CHECK reference passes, and
   skips empty aux-stream work on headless ranks (n_local_heads == 0).

Quality:
Output-changing only on affected empty-slice rank-split steps, restoring the
same RoPE arithmetic those rows receive in every other step size. Non-empty
single-chunk steps issue the same kernels on the same streams in the same
order. Measured in experiments/2026-11-23-decode-rope-empty-index-slice.

Tests:
- tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py: extend
  test_decode_two_stream_overlap_schedules_disjoint_workspaces to cover an
  empty rank-split slice (asserting rope(q) and decode_metadata run once on
  aux before gather and attend), a non-empty rank-split slice, multi-chunk
  scoring idempotence (DECODE_CHUNK=2 on 4 rows), and a headless rank
  (n_local_heads=0) dealt no index rows.

Upstream status: local DeepSeek V4.1 TileLang decode overlap; nothing to send
upstream.
